      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.25$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.15$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $0.05$ | $0.2$ | $0.05$ |\n\nCompute $P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)\\})$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above.",
      "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P((X,Y)\\in \\{(1,0),(1,2),(2,1),(3,2)\\}) & =P((X,Y)=(1,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(1,2)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(3,2)) \\\\  & =f(1,0)+f(1,2)+f(2,1)+f(3,2) \\\\  & =0.05+0.25+0.05+0.05 \\\\  & =0.4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
